### TrustLedger: get a Keycloak token for each test user, then call GET /api/v1/ping.
# IntelliJ HTTP Client. Select the "local" environment.
# One-time setup:
#   1. .env has TRUSTLEDGER_DEV_USER_PASSWORD and TRUSTLEDGER_DEV_TOTP_SECRET (see .env.example),
#      and Keycloak was (re)created after setting them:
#        docker compose -f infra/docker-compose.yml up -d --force-recreate keycloak
#   2. Copy http-client.private.env.json.example to http-client.private.env.json (git-ignored)
#      and put the same password in it.
#   3. Run core-app with the local profile.
# The trustledger-dev client (password grant) exists for LOCAL TESTING ONLY. Tokens live 5 minutes.
#
# officer1, officer2 and admin1 need a current 6-digit TOTP code (OTP is required for staff).
# Generate one, paste it into @otp below, and run that user's request within 30 seconds.
# A code can be used only once, so generate a new one for each staff login:
#   oathtool --totp -b "$(printf '%s' "$TRUSTLEDGER_DEV_TOTP_SECRET" | base32)"
# (or add the base32 secret to an authenticator app once).

@otp = 000000
@token_url = {{keycloak}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token

### customer1: token
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=trustledger-dev&username=customer1&password={{password}}

> {%
    client.test("customer1 got a token", () => client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status));
    client.global.set("customer1_token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### customer1: ping -> 200, roles [CUSTOMER]
GET {{api}}/api/v1/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### customer1: own profile -> 200, masked; the first call creates the user row (JIT provisioning)
# {"id":"...","email":"c***@example.test","phone":null,"fullName":"T*** C*** O***","status":"ACTIVE","roles":["CUSTOMER"]}
GET {{api}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### customer1: consents -> requiredGiven=false at first; policyVersions shows what to send
GET {{api}}/api/v1/me/consents
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### customer1: accept TERMS and PRIVACY, opt in to MARKETING -> 201
POST {{api}}/api/v1/me/consents
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"consents":[
  {"purpose":"TERMS","policyVersion":"2026-11-01","granted":true},
  {"purpose":"PRIVACY","policyVersion":"2026-11-01","granted":true},
  {"purpose":"MARKETING","policyVersion":"2026-11-01","granted":true}
]}

### customer1: withdraw MARKETING -> 201, a new history row (nothing is overwritten)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/me/consents
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"consents":[{"purpose":"MARKETING","policyVersion":"2026-11-01","granted":false}]}

### customer1: try to withdraw TERMS -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED (required consent)
POST {{api}}/api/v1/me/consents
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"consents":[{"purpose":"TERMS","policyVersion":"2026-11-01","granted":false}]}

### customer1: transfer stub -> 501 NOT_IMPLEMENTED (until M6). Run 21 times within a minute:
### the 21st gets 429 RATE_LIMITED with Retry-After. X-RateLimit-Remaining counts down.
POST {{api}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### customer2: token
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=trustledger-dev&username=customer2&password={{password}}

> {% client.global.set("customer2_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### customer2: ping -> 200, roles [CUSTOMER]
GET {{api}}/api/v1/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2_token}}

### officer1: password only -> 400 invalid_grant (OTP is required)
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=trustledger-dev&username=officer1&password={{password}}

### officer1: token (paste a fresh code into @otp first)
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=trustledger-dev&username=officer1&password={{password}}&totp={{otp}}

> {% client.global.set("officer1_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### officer1: ping -> 200, roles [COMPLIANCE_OFFICER]
GET {{api}}/api/v1/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### officer2: token (fresh code into @otp first)
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=trustledger-dev&username=officer2&password={{password}}&totp={{otp}}

> {% client.global.set("officer2_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### officer2: ping -> 200, roles [COMPLIANCE_OFFICER]
GET {{api}}/api/v1/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{officer2_token}}

### admin1: token (fresh code into @otp first)
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=trustledger-dev&username=admin1&password={{password}}&totp={{otp}}

> {% client.global.set("admin1_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### admin1: ping -> 200, roles [ADMIN]
GET {{api}}/api/v1/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{admin1_token}}

### auditor1: token
POST {{token_url}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=trustledger-dev&username=auditor1&password={{password}}

> {% client.global.set("auditor1_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### auditor1: ping -> 200, roles [AUDITOR]
GET {{api}}/api/v1/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{auditor1_token}}

### No token -> 401 ProblemDetail (UNAUTHENTICATED) with WWW-Authenticate: Bearer
GET {{api}}/api/v1/ping

### Wrong role: customer1 on an admin path -> 403 ProblemDetail (ACCESS_DENIED)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/reconciliation/run
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### Public: health needs no token -> 200
GET {{api}}/actuator/health
